{"repositoryId":1254689045,"availability":"available","full":"bemtvi/bemtvi","name":"bemtvi","description":"A fast and extensible vim-style editor","category":"Developer tools","language":"Rust","stars":3,"forks":1,"created":"2026-05-30T22:13:59Z","updated":"2026-10-18T16:26:24Z","license":"Apache-2.0","branch":"main","homepage":"https://bemtvi.github.io/bemtvi/","topics":["editor","modal-editing","neovim","vim"],"demo":"https://bemtvi.github.io/bemtvi/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-19T18:04:20.180Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-19T18:04:20.180Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-19T18:04:20.180Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-19T18:04:20.180Z","stars":3,"forks":1}],"technologies":["Rust"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["bemtvi (pronounced ben-tee-vee) is a modal, vim-style editor architected from scratch — modal editing, Lua plugins, treesitter highlighting, and LSP, built on a fully async, client-server design.","You may be thinking: why another editor instead of using or improving neovim?","Neovim is amazing. It was my main editor for a while, and bemtvi owes it a lot: the client-server split, Lua as the config language, built-in treesitter and LSP. But some of neovim's limits come from decisions built into its core, and rewriting parts of it in faster C or Rust won't remove them. I tried working around them. In the end, fixing them meant starting again from a clean slate."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/bemtvi/bemtvi/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"d9da7457f0ee618cd79288b76d56c4dbd50ccbe59a27ba2124d771fa622f1798","extractedAt":"2026-10-19T18:04:20.288Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-19T18:04:20.288Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"bemtvi (pronounced ben-tee-vee) is a modal, vim-style editor architected from scratch — modal editing, Lua plugins, treesitter highlighting, and LSP, built on a fully async, client-server design.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/bemtvi/bemtvi/blob/main/READ